From 04a14c5df4c1211651af5e05ae54864d3e8f5b34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 13:16:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08096/11362] [outer-loop] Artifact builder + a probe for why
 the seeded sampler does not reproduce

Written while collection runs, so the analysis path is fixed before the numbers
land rather than shaped by them.

determinism_probe.py isolates WHICH factor breaks reproducibility, in four
conditions each one change apart: short/cached, long/cached back-to-back,
long/cached with another prompt between (the A/B's actual access pattern), and
long/uncached. If B matches and C does not, prefix reuse across a changed cache
state is the cause; if D then matches, cache_prompt is the mechanism. It runs
AFTER collection against the same server -- running it during would inject
requests into the very cache whose reuse is under suspicion.

The probe's own caveat is stated in it: one replicate per condition, so a match
is weak evidence of determinism and a MISMATCH is strong evidence against it.
Read the mismatches.

build_artifact.py reads analysis.json and recomputes nothing, so the artifact
and the detail files cannot disagree by two independent derivations. Its
acceptance gates ask whether the RUN could answer its question, never whether
the answer was the hoped-for one -- and the positive control (did the treatment
ACT, measured as the excess re-ask rate in the ON arm) gates how any null may be
read at all.

No default flipped. No scored or online ARC game played.

